Critical issues (must fix)
[P2] ProjectHost asset failure bypasses listener/service cleanup.
plugins/auto-research-agent/cli/research_workspace_native/project_host.py:75-83 calls AtlasHost.__init__ before reading projects.html, projects.js, projects.css and projects-library.js. The superclass opens/binds the listener through http.py:70, then transfers native_runtime/harness_ops/stage_actions ownership at atlas_host.py:390-393. A missing or unreadable project asset raises afterwards, leaving construction incomplete and skipping the only owned-service cleanup in atlas_host.py:426-453. ProjectHost.main leaves host=None when construction raises, so project_host.py:459-460 also cannot call server_close. The caller has received no host handle and cannot perform that cleanup. This can retain an owned runtime or service/journal owner after a failed construction; eventual garbage collection is not the documented cleanup protocol.
Fix: preload all four project asset byte strings before calling super().__init__, then install those already-read bytes. Add a focused constructor regression that makes each project asset read fail and verifies the superclass is not invoked, so no listener opens and caller-supplied services remain borrowed. No constructor-failure case exists among the current nine ProjectHostTests methods; their teardown only closes successful construction.

